Workers, hosted runs, and supplied-bundle runs remain source-only; assess changed tests and contracts from source. Only a native local coordinator without a supplied bundle may optionally run a minimal test or repro under SKILL.md's detached-worktree validation rules: use a temporary detached worktree at manifest.target.head, never execute target code in the developer checkout or bundle, record the exact command and result, and remove the temporary worktree and scratch files afterwards. If optional validation is unavailable, record the reason and remain source-only without reporting INCOMPLETE.